WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.300
A glucose molecule holds 6 carbon atoms.

2
00:00:03.350 --> 00:00:06.790
First, it is split into
2 pyruvate molecules,

3
00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:08.650
each with 3 carbons.

4
00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:12.140
Then each pyruvate is
carried across two membranes,

5
00:00:12.190 --> 00:00:13.880
into a mitochondrion.

6
00:00:13.930 --> 00:00:16.390
It goes in with 3 carbon atoms.

7
00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:19.600
So where do they go, and
what does the cell gain?

8
00:00:19.650 --> 00:00:22.480
In this mission, you'll
tour the mitochondrion:

9
00:00:22.530 --> 00:00:27.290
its two membranes, the folded
cristae, and the fluid matrix inside.

10
00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:31.730
Then you'll follow the Krebs cycle, a
loop of reactions that rebuilds its own

11
00:00:31.780 --> 00:00:34.600
starting molecule, ready to turn again.

12
00:00:34.650 --> 00:00:37.510
Your mission: track
the three carbon atoms,

13
00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:39.630
and find out what the cell gains.
